{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "WRF",
    "description": "WRF regridding model — the coupler half of the wrf loader+regridding-model split (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §6/§7; bead esm-3nc.1). Exposes WRF regional weather fields (UCAR RDA d340000, WRF-Chem v3.9.1 CONUS 12 km) on the simulation's target grid for advection and chemistry coupling in EarthSciML systems.\n\nStructure (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §6):\n  1. It declares the pure-I/O loader (components/earthsci_data/wrf_loader.esm) as the subsystem `raw` via {\"ref\": \"./wrf_loader.esm\"}. Loader fields are referenced as raw.<var> (e.g. raw.U) and re-exposed as model-level observed variables (WRF.U, WRF.V, ...) to preserve the runtime MeanWind coupling contract (WRF.U/V/W → MeanWind via WRFCoupler/couple2).\n  2. Reprojection: WRF's native grid is projected (lambert_conformal), so the coordinate transform is the LCC reproject (ESD reprojection/lambert_conformal.esm, esd-47z.2) — selected by convention from the loader's grid.crs.projection = 'lambert_conformal' and parameterized by the loader's crs parameters {lat_1:30, lat_2:60, lat_0:38.999996, lon_0:-97, R:6370000}.\n  3. Regridding (per variable, RFC §5.2): the Arakawa-C-grid wind components U, V, W are edge/face-staggered → B-spline interpolation; the cell-centered scalars T, PH, PHB, P, PB, QVAPOR → conservative (area-weighted, mass-conserving) regridding. Declared in the `regrid` block.\n\nTop-level derived quantities computed on the target grid: total pressure P_total = P + PB, geopotential height z = (PH + PHB)/g, and the lat/lon coordinate metrics δxδlon and δyδlat (emitted only for lat/lon coordinate domains).\n\nMeanWind coupling (from EarthSciData.jl@830435a coupling.jl): MeanWind.v_lon ~ WRF.U, MeanWind.v_lat ~ WRF.V, MeanWind.v_lev ~ WRF.W.\n\nMigrated from EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/wrf.jl:169 (WRF constructor, esm-4l84); split into pure loader + regridding model by esm-3nc.1.",
    "tags": [
      "earthsci_data",
      "meteorology",
      "atmospheric_dynamics",
      "regridding_model",
      "regional_climate",
      "wrf",
      "conus",
      "lambert_conformal"
    ],
    "created": "2026-06-25T00:00:00Z",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciData.jl contributors",
      "EarthSciModels migration (esm-3nc.1)"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Skamarock, W. C., Klemp, J. B., Dudhia, J., Gill, D. O., Liu, Z., Berner, J., Wang, W., Powers, J. G., Duda, M. G., Barker, D. M., and Huang, X.-Y. (2021). A Description of the Advanced Research WRF Model Version 4.3. NCAR Tech. Note NCAR/TN-556+STR, doi:10.5065/1dfh-6p97.",
        "url": "https://www2.mmm.ucar.edu/wrf/users/"
      },
      {
        "citation": "UCAR Research Data Archive, dataset d340000. WRF-Chem v3.9.1 CONUS 12 km hourly output, May 2019 – May 2026. https://rda.ucar.edu/datasets/d340000/",
        "url": "https://rda.ucar.edu/datasets/d340000/"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Source: EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/wrf.jl:169 (WRFFileSet struct, WRF constructor). Test: test/wrf_test.jl."
      }
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "WRF": {
      "coupletype": "WRFCoupler",
      "reference": {
        "notes": "source_ref: EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/wrf.jl:169\n\nThis is the regridding-model half of the pure-IO loader migration (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §6/§7, bead esm-3nc.1). The pre-migration wrf.esm carried both the coupler model AND a co-located data_loaders.WRF_hourly_d01 block (with the now-removed `spatial` and `regridding` sub-blocks). That loader is now the pure-I/O file components/earthsci_data/wrf_loader.esm, referenced here as subsystem `raw`.\n\nUpstream WRF(domaininfo; name=:WRF, stream=true, spatial_interp=:linear) created an MTK System with:\n  - @parameters: lon/lat (rad) when pvars include :lat/:lon, or x/y (m) when pvars include :x/:y; lev (1); t_ref (s)\n  - For every varname in WRFFileSet.varnames(fs), one DataSetInterpolator and one observed equation via create_interp_equation (uses interp_unsafe). These are now provided by the loader subsystem `raw` (raw.<var>) and re-exposed as model observed variables U/V/W/T/PH/PHB/P/PB/QVAPOR for the coupling contract.\n  - Staggered grids: PH/PHB/W on bottom_top_stag (N+1 z-points), U on west_east_stag (N+1 x-points), V on south_north_stag (N+1 y-points); the upstream loader de-staggers to mass centres in loadmetadata. In the new pipeline the native staggered dimensions are preserved on the loader's GDD grid and the wind components are regridded with a B-spline kernel (RFC §5.2).\n  - Extrapolation: W uses extrapolate_type=0.0 (zero below ground); all others use Flat() (clamp).\n  - Derived observed variables: P_total ~ P + PB; z ~ (PH + PHB)/g with g=9.80665 m/s²; δxδlon ~ lon2m·cos(lat) and δyδlat ~ lat2meters (only when :lat in pvdict), lon2m = 40075e3/(2π) ≈ 6378134.3, lat2meters = 111.32e3·180/π ≈ 6378166.0.\n  - couple2 with MeanWindCoupler: maps WRF.U/V/W → MeanWind v_lon/v_lat/v_lev via _couple_meanwind.\n\nReprojection (RFC §6 step 2): WRF's native grid.crs.projection is 'lambert_conformal', so the reprojection rule selected by convention is ESD reprojection/lambert_conformal.esm (esd-47z.2), parameterized by the loader crs parameters {lat_1:30, lat_2:60, lat_0:38.999996, lon_0:-97} on a sphere of radius R=6370000 m. The projected-grid construction (corner geometry via inverse LCC) is ESD discretizations/grids/lambert_conformal/wrf_lcc.esm (esd-47z.5).\n\nRegridding (RFC §6 step 3 / §5.2): declared per variable in the model `regrid` block. The Arakawa-C-grid wind components U (west_east_stag), V (south_north_stag), W (bottom_top_stag) are edge/face-staggered → B-spline interpolating regridder (ESD regridding/bspline_regrid.esm, esd-47z.3). The cell-centered scalars T, PH, PHB, P, PB, QVAPOR → conservative area-weighted overlap join (ESD regridding/conservative_regrid_overlap_join.esm). (PH/PHB are geopotential scalars even though they reside on the staggered w-levels; they are mass-like quantities regridded conservatively.)\n\nδzδlev gap (gt-p3ep(lookup)): evaluating PH and PHB at lev+1 requires the indexed-offset form of loader evaluation (a gt-p3ep(lookup) expression) not yet representable in the ESM expression language. δzδlev is omitted from this migration. When gt-p3ep(lookup) is resolved, add δzδlev = (raw.PH@lev+1 + raw.PHB@lev+1 - raw.PH - raw.PHB)/9.80665.\n\nCoordinate system: this ESM targets the lat/lon coordinate form (pvars contain :lat and :lon). For LCC-projected (x/y) domains the loader uses pvars :x and :y; δxδlon/δyδlat are not emitted in that case.\n\nLive tests (informational; require UCAR RDA NetCDF files, not run in CI): EarthSciData.jl wrf_test.jl expected values at (lon=-118.2707°, lat=34.0059°):\n  P_total at lev=[1,1.5,2,21.5,30,31.5]: [100331.86, 100235.72, 100139.58, 67846.08, 30679.47, 28729.87] Pa\n  W at lev=[0.5,1,1.5,2,21.5,30,31.5]: [0.0, 5.205e-3, 1.041e-2, 1.164e-2, -1.698e-2, 2.697e-2, 2.244e-2] m/s"
      },
      "tolerance": {
        "rel": 1e-06
      },
      "variables": {
        "lon": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "rad",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Longitude of the model grid point (radians). Coupled to the simulation domain's longitude coordinate via param_to_var when composed into a CoupledSystem. Used as the x-axis coordinate for WRF data interpolation in lat/lon domains."
        },
        "lat": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "rad",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Latitude of the model grid point (radians). Coupled to the simulation domain's latitude coordinate via param_to_var when composed into a CoupledSystem. Used as the y-axis coordinate for WRF data interpolation in lat/lon domains."
        },
        "lev": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "Vertical level index (dimensionless, 1-based integer corresponding to the WRF bottom_top layer). Fractional values interpolate between layers. Coupled from the simulation domain's lev coordinate."
        },
        "t_ref": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "s",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Reference epoch (seconds since the Julian date epoch) from which the WRF file time axis is offset. Set from DomainInfo.get_tref(domaininfo) at construction time."
        },
        "U": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m/s",
          "description": "Zonal (west–east) wind component (m/s). Sourced from the loader field raw.U (WRF variable U on the west_east_stag C-grid edges), regridded with a B-spline kernel. Coupled to MeanWind.v_lon via WRFCoupler/couple2."
        },
        "V": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m/s",
          "description": "Meridional (south–north) wind component (m/s). Sourced from the loader field raw.V (WRF variable V on the south_north_stag C-grid edges), regridded with a B-spline kernel. Coupled to MeanWind.v_lat via WRFCoupler/couple2."
        },
        "W": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m/s",
          "description": "Vertical wind component (m/s). Sourced from the loader field raw.W (WRF variable W on the bottom_top_stag C-grid edges), regridded with a B-spline kernel. Zero-extrapolated below the surface in the upstream loader. Coupled to MeanWind.v_lev via WRFCoupler/couple2."
        },
        "T": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "description": "Perturbation potential temperature (K). Full potential temperature θ = T + 300 K. Cell-centred (mass grid), conservatively regridded. Sourced from raw.T."
        },
        "PH": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m^2/s^2",
          "description": "Perturbation geopotential (m² s⁻²). On the w-level (bottom_top_stag) grid. PH + PHB gives total geopotential. Sourced from raw.PH."
        },
        "PHB": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m^2/s^2",
          "description": "Base-state geopotential (m² s⁻²). On the w-level (bottom_top_stag) grid. PH + PHB gives total geopotential. Sourced from raw.PHB."
        },
        "P": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "Pa",
          "description": "Perturbation pressure (Pa). Cell-centred (mass grid). P + PB gives total atmospheric pressure. Sourced from raw.P."
        },
        "PB": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "Pa",
          "description": "Base-state pressure (Pa). Cell-centred (mass grid). P + PB gives total atmospheric pressure. Sourced from raw.PB."
        },
        "QVAPOR": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "description": "Water vapor mixing ratio (kg water per kg dry air). Cell-centred (mass grid). Sourced from raw.QVAPOR."
        },
        "P_total": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "Pa",
          "description": "Total atmospheric pressure (Pa): P_total = P + PB. Sum of perturbation and base-state pressure components, both on the mass grid. Computed from the loader fields raw.P and raw.PB."
        },
        "z": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "Geopotential height (m): z = (PH + PHB) / g, where g = 9.80665 m s⁻². Computed from the w-level geopotential components. Corresponds to the upstream z ~ (PH_itp + PHB_itp) / g_const equation."
        },
        "δxδlon": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m/rad",
          "description": "Coordinate metric: x-distance per unit longitude (m rad⁻¹). δxδlon = lon2m·cos(lat) where lon2m = 40075×10³/(2π) ≈ 6378134 m rad⁻¹ (equatorial circumference metric). Non-zero only in lat/lon coordinate domains; the upstream constructor emits this equation only when :lat is in DomainInfo.pvars."
        },
        "δyδlat": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m/rad",
          "description": "Coordinate metric: y-distance per unit latitude (m rad⁻¹). δyδlat = lat2meters = 111.32×10³·(180/π) ≈ 6378166 m rad⁻¹. Constant (does not depend on position). Emitted only in lat/lon coordinate domains."
        }
      },
      "subsystems": {
        "raw": {
          "ref": "./wrf_loader.esm"
        }
      },
      "regrid": {
        "U": {
          "method": "bspline",
          "description": "Zonal wind on west_east_stag (Arakawa-C x-edges). Edge-staggered C-grid wind → B-spline interpolating regridder (ESD regridding/bspline_regrid.esm, esd-47z.3)."
        },
        "V": {
          "method": "bspline",
          "description": "Meridional wind on south_north_stag (Arakawa-C y-edges). Edge-staggered C-grid wind → B-spline interpolating regridder (esd-47z.3)."
        },
        "W": {
          "method": "bspline",
          "description": "Vertical wind on bottom_top_stag (Arakawa-C z-edges). Face-staggered C-grid wind → B-spline interpolating regridder (esd-47z.3)."
        },
        "T": {
          "method": "conservative",
          "description": "Perturbation potential temperature (K). Cell-centered scalar → conservative area-weighted overlap-join regridder (ESD regridding/conservative_regrid_overlap_join.esm)."
        },
        "PH": {
          "method": "conservative",
          "description": "Perturbation geopotential (m²/s²). A geopotential scalar (mass-like quantity, regridded conservatively even though it resides on the staggered w-levels)."
        },
        "PHB": {
          "method": "conservative",
          "description": "Base-state geopotential (m²/s²). A geopotential scalar → conservative regridder (see PH)."
        },
        "P": {
          "method": "conservative",
          "description": "Perturbation pressure (Pa). Cell-centered scalar → conservative regridder."
        },
        "PB": {
          "method": "conservative",
          "description": "Base-state pressure (Pa). Cell-centered scalar → conservative regridder."
        },
        "QVAPOR": {
          "method": "conservative",
          "description": "Water vapor mixing ratio (kg/kg). Cell-centered scalar → conservative regridder."
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": "U",
          "rhs": "raw.U"
        },
        {
          "lhs": "V",
          "rhs": "raw.V"
        },
        {
          "lhs": "W",
          "rhs": "raw.W"
        },
        {
          "lhs": "T",
          "rhs": "raw.T"
        },
        {
          "lhs": "PH",
          "rhs": "raw.PH"
        },
        {
          "lhs": "PHB",
          "rhs": "raw.PHB"
        },
        {
          "lhs": "P",
          "rhs": "raw.P"
        },
        {
          "lhs": "PB",
          "rhs": "raw.PB"
        },
        {
          "lhs": "QVAPOR",
          "rhs": "raw.QVAPOR"
        },
        {
          "lhs": "P_total",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "+",
            "args": [
              "raw.P",
              "raw.PB"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "z",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "+",
                "args": [
                  "raw.PH",
                  "raw.PHB"
                ]
              },
              9.80665
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "δxδlon",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              6378134.3,
              {
                "op": "cos",
                "args": [
                  "lat"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "δyδlat",
          "rhs": 6378166.0
        }
      ],
      "tests": []
    }
  }
}
